Z||000018||Monkeyman||01-08-2000||07:03 AM||||2birds--The Navy might have nuclear power,but the Army gets to blow up rouge nuclear power plants!!  Besides, if your ship get blown up in the middle of the ocean, how are you gonna get home?  If my Jeep blows up I can walk!  Just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Formula||01-08-2000||01:46 PM||||The GLHS was shelby's version of the charger after he broke away from dodge. Its the same as the Shelby Dodge Charger. I don't know if the Omni GLH was ever called the GLHS or not.  I still see a shelby daytona every once and a while and a rusted out charger with the shelby stickers on the side, but it doesn't have the mean looking front end that my dads Shelby Dodge Charger had. We also had one of the Omni GLH's but I was too young to remember either of them.<P>IMHO, an 11 year old v6 is going to be better then an 11 year old turbo 4.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Eric||01-08-2000||03:41 PM||||I raced him again yesterday and beat him.  We were coming up to a light so I got beside him.  The light turned green and I left him a car length behind as he smoked his tires up.  I never really pulled away though.  He was there all the way up to sixty when I backed of it.  I parked my Fiero and jumped in his Shadow (V6 normally aspirated manual tranny, like mine) with my GTech performance meter.  With an extra 170 lbs in the car he was able to get the car to sixty in 7.8 seconds and through the quarter in 16.2.  My best 0-60 run without and passengers was about 7.1 seconds.  Other than that, he may be able to extract a few more ponies from his car because he drives it a little harder than I do with my Fiero.  I guess a wallet that's $2500 lighter makes your right foot a little weaker.||||reg||1
Z||000021||2birds||01-08-2000||11:29 PM||||A guy on my boat has an '85 Chrysler Laser (Dodge Daytona with leather seats), with the Turbo 2.2 4-banger/5-speed.  Around the same mileage as my 86 GT (160,000 plus miles) and it is very quick, especially after the turbo lag goes away.  He takes pretty good care of it (typical submarine nuke, if it ain't broke, fix it anyway!). And I agree with Formula about the durability of the average blown motor, or I would have kept my Supercoupe. <P>And Monkeyman, if my boat gets blown up, there probably won't be any world left to come back to.  Nice thought, huh?||||reg||1
Z||000022||Monkeyman||01-09-2000||05:54 AM||||Formula-the GLHS was an Omni.  Just a hotter version than the GLH.||||reg||1
